"concrete.", "s": 43.348, "e": 44.149}], "sentences": [{"text": "Did you know ancient Roman concrete is actually stronger than the concrete we use today?", "s": 0.05, "e": 5.957}, {"text": "Modern steel-reinforced concrete crumbles after about 50 to 100 years when exposed to saltwater.", "s": 6.137, "e": 14.209}, {"text": "Yet Roman harbors built 2,000 years ago are still standing, and growing harder.", "s": 14.329, "e": 19.751}, {"text": "Scientists discovered the secret: Romans mixed volcanic ash, quicklime, and seawater.", "s": 19.871, "e": 25.868}, {"text": "When ocean water seeps into tiny cracks, it reacts with the volcanic minerals to grow microscopic interlocking crystals that actually seal the fractures from the inside out.", "s": 25.988, "e": 38.178}, {"text": "Nature destroys modern concrete, while the ocean literally heals Roman concrete.", "s": 38.298, "e": 44.149}]}